  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 214 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nThe extended forecast will feature much of the same weather expected \non Sunday. Placement on the backside of persistent upper-level \ntroughing will keep CAA in place through the early part of the week. \nWhile the resulting subsidence will promote dry weather, highs on \nMonday and Tuesday are progged to only reach into the mid to upper \n30s, with overnight lows ranging from the teens to the lower 20s. By \nWednesday, a shortwave trough will begin to dig out of western \nCanada, inducing downstream upper-level ridging and height rises \nover the region. This synoptic shift will maintain dry conditions \nwhile initiating a relative warming trend, with daytime highs \nclimbing back into the mid to upper 40s beginning Wednesday and \npersisting through the remainder of the week.",
